wer/scc-module-specs (lh/registry)\ntest/yang/php/antlr/prelude_test.cljc:20:  (into (conj (prelude/defined-keys prelude/uast) 'yin/def)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3871:      :primitives (core-module/free-primitives :yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:4149:    (core-module/scc-module-specs\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:4153:                (core-module/alias-spec (path-module-symbol name) module-exports\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc:6:   `lower/scc-module-specs` emitters and site sets; no binder table.\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc:41:   :scc-module-specs lower/scc-module-specs,\ntest/yang/php/antlr/siteset_test.clj:128:                :primitives (module/free-primitives :test/error :test/undeclared\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_emitter_test.clj:72:    (is (= '#{entry} (core-prelude/defined-keys (:ast spec))))))\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc:33:  (prelude/wide-app operands))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc:6:   `lower/module-spec` and `lower/scc-module-specs` emitters, the I7 site\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc:36:                       (lower/scc-module-specs registry units py-address call-address deps)),\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:3781:  core/defined-keys)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2304:  (core-module/declare-free-name :yang.python.antlr/refusal\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2467:    (core-module/scc-module-specs\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2471:                (core-module/alias-spec (module-symbol name) module-exports\n(ns yang.core.uast\n  \"Universal AST constructors shared by every language lowering and prelude. Every\n   function returns a canonical map node (`:literal`, `:variable`, `:lambda`,\n   `:application`, `:if`, `:vm/current-continuation`); nothing here adds a\n   node type.\n\n   `sexp->uast` reads a small s-expression notation into those same nodes so\n   the prelude can be written legibly:\n\n     symbol            -> :variable\n     (fn [params] b)   -> :lambda\n     (if t c a)        -> :if\n     (do a b ... z)    -> sequencing through one-parameter lambdas\n     (let [x v ...] b) -> nested immediately applied lambdas\n     (quote x)         -> :literal x\n     (%capture)        -> :vm/current-continuation\n     (yin/def k v)     -> the definition application\n     (f a ...)         -> :application\n     any other value   -> :literal\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn lit\n  [x]\n  {:type :literal, :value x})\n\n\n(defn v\n  [sym]\n  {:type :variable, :name sym})\n\n\n(defn lam\n  [params body]\n  {:type :lambda, :params (vec params), :body body})\n\n\n(defn app\n  [op & args]\n  {:type :application, :operator op, :operands (vec args)})\n\n\n(defn if-node\n   Generated names come from CST node ids (`%brk17`, `%w17`, ...): unique per\n   node, deterministic, and `%` cannot begin a Python identifier. Guest\n   locals keep their Python names in the lexical env and lowered code names\n   only `py/`, `cell/`, `%` names and non-identifier primitives (`=`,\n   `+`), so no guest name can shadow a primitive or prelude name. It never\n   names a runtime key (`py.b/*`, `py.rt/*`): an implicit class base is\n   `(py/object-class)`.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as p]\n    [yang.core.lower :as core]\n    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n    [yang.core.stage :as core-stage]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.scope :as scope]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n\n\n(ns yang.clojure.prelude\n  \"The `clj` runtime module (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.10):\n   the published linker module every linked clojure program requires, as\n   `js`, `php` and `py` are for their frontends. It is written in prelude\n   notation and emitted with the same core machinery those preludes use;\n   it never runs on the host.\n\n   Three surfaces, mirroring the other runtimes:\n\n   - the entry, `clj/run-main`: initialize the runtime state, run the\n     unit — the thunk `yang.clojure/lower-unit` lowered — and answer the\n     program's value with the outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]`\n     wrapper removed, since that wrapper is frontend-internal. The\n     entry does not reset the global namespace: the namespace lives for\n     the task, so a projection the composition bound between two\n     entries and a definition an earlier unit published both survive\n     into the next unit's run (as `js/run-main` leaves `globalThis`\n     standing);\n   - the runtime global namespace, `clj/define-global!` and\n     `clj/global-get`: a task-local map in a cell (`clj.rt/globals`,\n     allocated once per task by `clj/init!`), keyed by export name. A\n     program's top-level definitions land here through its unit's own\n     publishing, and the conformance helper's export projection reads\n     and writes it — the one binding a linked unit reads a projected or\n     defined name through. A definition a unit runs publishes after\n     any projection of the same name and shadows it. The JS\n     `globalThis` table, the PHP named-function table and the Python\n     module dictionary are the same seam;\n   - the continuation family, `clj/try`, `clj/try-finally`, `clj/throw`,\n     `clj/raise` and its helpers: the\n     `%capture` handler-stack scheme the py/ts/php preludes carry, over a\n     dynamic-context cell `clj.rt/ctx` (allocated by `clj/init!`). It is\n     the reference implementation yang.clojure's exception lowering\n     converges onto (R3, section 8.10.7); the consumer wiring that calls\n     these entries lands after the family exists;\n   - admission, `admit`: the registry surface a linked clojure composition\n     needs beside the others — the `kind` module and the `portable`\n     adapters of the data exports the guest library's collection\n     predicates read.\n\n   The module pins the shared calling runtime (`yang.call`) at the\n   convention's call-address, as the other runtimes do, and refuses before\n   anything is published when a free name nothing supplies is read.\"\n  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.prelude-admission :as prelude-admission]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n(ns yang.python.antlr.siteset\n  \"C4 slice I7 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6, ruling 14): published site\n   sets for imported modules.\n\n   Site marks never enter canonical rows, so a published module tree\n   carries none; they live in the frontend-metadata side table. A module's\n   site set is that side table's `:yang/site` marks for the module tree,\n   sorted (`yang.safepoint/site-set`) and content-addressed. A separate\n   publication record, keyed by the module's manifest address, pins the\n   association: the exact code root (the manifest's `:yin.module/tree`),\n   the frontend revision, the transformation profile and the set's\n   address. The module manifest keeps its schema: a manifest address names\n   code, and a record names a manifest.\n\n   Discovery. The publisher signs a publication entry per module,\n   `{:yang.site/manifest m :yang.site/record record-address ...}`, and\n   indexes it as the datoms `[e :yang.site/envelope env]` and `[e\n   :yang.site/proof proof]` beside its name envelopes (`signed-entry`).\n   A reader `discover`s a manifest's record addresses from the index\n   datoms it loaded, under the principals it declares; only a declared\n   principal's signature makes an entry count. The record and the set are\n   fetched by address and verified against it.\n\n   A consumer under a profile requiring hooks `admit`s an import: it\n   verifies every pin against the published code root and refuses a\n   missing, empty or mismatched set, naming the profile and the set.\n   `stage` then applies a verified set at link time, as the linker\n   composition's `:stage`: it derives the instrumented module `A'` from the\n   published tree alone, bottom-up over the module's guest requirements,\n   and publishes it beside its `:derive` record. An explicitly noninterruptible profile imports the module\n   as published, with none.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.core.siteset-store :as store]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
